+#### Preparation V2 Evidence Boundary
+
+`POST /api/recipes/{id}/export-view/prepare` calls the existing
+`analyzeRecipeText('', preparationContext)` once. With context, its system
+message is exclusively `RECIPE_PREPARATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT` v2; without context,
+free-text import keeps the unchanged v15 prompt. JSON is sent only in the user
+message: `recipeContext` projects saved metadata and ingredient values without
+stored ingredient IDs, while `steps` preserves stored array order and
+`order`/`title`/`description`. The prompt requests unchanged model source steps
+(missing title becomes `null`), not fresh source extraction.
+
+The full `AiRecipeRaw` output remains required by the unchanged
+`recipe_analyze` Strict schema, including ingredients and ingredient keys.
+Model selection, temperature 0.2, max_tokens 2048, and one provider call remain
+unchanged; no new client operation, retry, fallback, or intermediate output.
+The v2 prompt requests content-driven adjacent grouping only after accounting
+for every saved action/detail, under the existing five-step/90-character limits.
+This is prompt intent, not proof of content preservation or model causality.
+
+The handler replaces model-returned source steps with saved `recipe.steps`
+for `validateRecipeExportPreparationOutput()`. Invalid traces (missing,
+duplicate, unknown, or reordered references), empty text, nullable-metadata
+violations, and limits fail with `422`. The V2 response projects only export
+text; unused ingredient fields/key references do not block preparation, while
+import retains full validation. There is no general runtime content validator:
+valid IDs/counts/lengths can still accompany missing actions or details.
+Auth, optional ETag before quota, `429`/`502`, usage only after valid success,
+privacy-safe bounded order diagnostics, and transience are unchanged.
